# Linler — Notion-like backend

Simplified Notion clone. Backend only (NestJS 11 + TypeORM + PostgreSQL, package manager: pnpm).
TypeORM runs with `synchronize: true` (no migrations yet — schema auto-syncs from entities).

## Teaching mode (IMPORTANT)

The author is a backend beginner building their first project and is learning NestJS/TypeORM
while we build. For every change:
- Add clear teaching comments IN RUSSIAN in the code that explain the WHY of non-obvious framework
  mechanics (TypeORM relations: `@ManyToOne`/`@OneToMany`, the two decorator callbacks,
  `@JoinColumn`, owning vs inverse side; NestJS pipes/guards/DI/`forwardRef`, validation flow,
  decorators). Comments go in entities, services, controllers, enums and DTOs.
- When introducing a new concept, explain it in the reply in plain language, referencing the exact
  file/lines. Prefer a short "why it works this way" over just "what it does".
- This overrides the usual "no narration comments" guidance: educational comments are wanted here.

## API response conventions

- Array/list endpoints must return an OBJECT envelope, never a bare array:
  `{ <itemsName>: [...] }` — e.g. `{ workspaces: [...] }`, `{ members: [...] }`,
  `{ invitations: [...] }`, `{ projects: [...] }`. Wrap at the controller boundary and use a
  dedicated `*ListResponseDto` so Swagger shows the shape. Single-object responses are returned as-is.

## Domain hierarchy

```
Workspace
  └── Projects
        ├── Project A
        │     ├── page
        │     └── page
        │           └── page (infinite nesting via parent_page_id)
        └── Project B
              └── page
```

- **Workspace** — top-level account/team container. Holds users, roles, projects, invitations, notifications.
- **Project** — container inside a workspace, shown as a top sidebar item. `visibility`: `PRIVATE` (owner + explicit project_members) or `WORKSPACE` (all active workspace members). Default = PRIVATE.
- **Page** — document inside a Project. Always belongs to a Project. `parent_page_id` (nullable) enables infinite nesting. Content stored as `jsonb` blocks.

## Access model

- A user can belong to multiple workspaces; each membership has a role.
- `workspace_members` roles: `OWNER | ADMIN | MEMBER | VIEWER`; status: `ACTIVE | SUSPENDED | LEFT`. Unique `(workspace_id, user_id)`.
- `project_members` roles: `OWNER | EDITOR | VIEWER`. Unique `(project_id, user_id)`. Lets a plain workspace MEMBER be EDITOR/VIEWER on a specific private project.
- Private projects are hidden from the workspace; only owner + project members see them. Workspace OWNER/ADMIN can administer/see project metadata in admin/moderation mode.
- Creating a private project in someone's workspace requires `CREATE_PRIVATE_PROJECT` permission.
- On registration: auto-create a workspace ("<Username>'s Workspace") and add the user to `workspace_members` as `OWNER`.

## Data model (planned tables)

users, user_sessions (done) ·
workspaces, workspace_members, workspace_invitations ·
projects, project_members ·
pages ·
tasks, task_statuses, task_assignees, task_comments, task_activity_logs ·
notifications

Key columns:
- **workspaces**: id, name, slug, owner_id, created_at, updated_at
- **workspace_members**: id, workspace_id, user_id, role, status, joined_at, updated_at
- **projects**: id, workspace_id, owner_id, name, icon, description, visibility, order_index, is_archived, created_at, updated_at
- **project_members**: id, project_id, user_id, role, created_at, updated_at
- **pages**: id, project_id, parent_page_id, created_by_id, updated_by_id, title, icon, content (jsonb), order_index, is_archived, created_at, updated_at

Pages later power 3 table views: kanban/drag-by-date board, table view, and column view.

## Code conventions (match existing code)

- Entities: `@Entity('snake_case_table')`, uuid PK via `@PrimaryGeneratedColumn('uuid')`, snake_case column `name`, `@CreateDateColumn({ name: 'created_at' })` / `@UpdateDateColumn`.
- One Nest module per domain (`src/<domain>/`): `*.module.ts`, `*.controller.ts`, `*.service.ts`, `entities/`, `dto/`.
- Services inject repos via `@InjectRepository`. Throw Nest exceptions with messages from `src/constants/error.constants.ts`.
- Protect routes with `@UseGuards(AccessTokenGuard)` + `@ApiAuth()`, read user via `@CurrentUser()`.

## Branch strategy

Build the model incrementally, one domain per branch (easier review + deployable steps).
- **workspace domain** (done): workspaces, workspace_members, workspace_invitations + auto-create-workspace-on-register + in-app invitation inbox (accept by id/token, decline).
- **projects domain** (done): projects, project_members with visibility PRIVATE/WORKSPACE.
  Access model (highest wins): workspace OWNER/ADMIN -> project OWNER (moderation);
  explicit project_members role; WORKSPACE visibility -> EDITOR (VIEWER for workspace viewers);
  PRIVATE with none of the above -> hidden.
- Later branches: pages → tasks/* → notifications.
- Email sending for invitations is intentionally deferred (in-app inbox covers it).
